t suspect that  wesley is enlisting her to be a traveler  it seems more likely that corey was  recruited to be the next supervisor  could corey be assigned a new subject to  monitor in 2024 or some other time  period could we see wesley and corey  return in the kind of spin-off that gary  7 was created for a show about a time  traveling agent watching over important  historical events producer alex kurtzman  has teased some upcoming mystery  projects in the star trek universe and  this is one that definitely seems like a  possibility cristobal chris rios was  introduced as a rogue captain in the  first season of picard he left starfleet  under shadowy circumstances following a  scandal and cover-up and went on to  become an independent operator  captaining the starship la sirena at the  end of the first season he returned to  starfleet now commander of the uss  stargazer captain rios is transported  back in time to 2024 alongside picard  rafi jaradi and seven of nine rios falls  in love with a 21st century woman named  teresa a doctor and mother running a  clinic in los angeles in the 25th  century gainan confirms that rios lived  out his life there starting a medical  supply company but is this really the  end of ryo's story if star trek has  taught us anything surprise returns are  the order of the day we know that la  sirena is equipped with a series of  holograms that uses ryosa's image so  it's not impossible that he could return  somewhere down the line as one of his  holographic assistants rios proved a  popular character with fans so there's a  good chance we haven't seen the last of  him yet  introduced in season 4 of star trek  voyager 7 of 9 has been on a journey  from being a villainous robotic drone  reliant on the borghive mind to becoming  a strong independent person who has  reclaimed her humanity in many small  steps  uh is something wrong  i am unaccustomed to this  borg do not sit  she expressed interest in joining  starfleet when the voyager crew returned  to the alpha quadrant wanting to follow  in captain janeway's footsteps in the  second season of picard we learned that  her dreams of federation service had  remained just that as starfleet rejected  her application thanks to her borg past  though fellow former drone up was  accepted spending her entire adult life  as a borg made starfleet wary of seven  in the finale of picard season two when  seven and the rest of picard's team  returned to the 25th century picard  gives her a field commission reasoning  that seven has the most experience with  the borg and is best suited to lead the  rest of the mission picard gives her the  captain's chair with the gerardi queen  and her unique borg collective now  requesting federation membership  combined with her field commission could  starfleet reconsider seven's application  actor jerry ryan has already made it  clear that she will appear in the series  third season and it's entirely possible  she could be a starfleet officer or a  borg ambassador when we see her next  during the next generation the  relationship between gainen and picard  was something of a mystery some of it  was resolved in the two-part episode  time's arrow in which picard traveled  back to 19th century earth and met  gainen from her perspective it was their  first meeting but all that changed in  picard leaving from an altered timeline  picard meets gainan in 2024 and for her  their encounter in the 1890s never  happened because the future picard left  from in times arrow no longer existed it  seemed that now their first meeting  occurred in 2024 i'll see you in 500  years but god and i'll see you  in a few minutes but with their mission  complete and the timeline from times  arrow now restored it would seem they've  met twice in the past in 1893 and again  in 2024. however in that version of 2024  she said she'd never met him so how  exactly does gainan's memory of picard  work are we now in a timeline where they  never met in the 19th century or is this  another case of infinite fragmented  timelines we're living through maybe  this is one question we shouldn't be  asking picard season 2 took the show's  crew on a mission to restore a timeline  fractured by q an important event in the  past had been changed and all of time  altered as a result we learned that it  centered on picard's ancestor renee an  astronaut who led a mission to europa in  2024 where she discovered a unique  organism without her missions success  all of time was rewritten and the future  twisted into a dark reality where  non-humans were subjugated by the  confederation and picard himself waged a  violent war of oppression but with this  organism new technologies would  apparently be developed that would  reverse all of the environmental damage  on earth the failure of the europa  mission meant the continued decimation  of the environment but it's not made  clear how that would have led to a  totalitarian world government in the  25th century nor does it explain why  adam sung would be known as an  anti-alien tyrant  the same galaxy  is a human galaxy  however in adam sung's timeline of 2024  first official contact with intelligent  alien life is still at least 40 years  away how did his conversations about the  future with jaradi and q lead him to  take such an aggressive anti-alien  stance and why was it embraced before  humanity had met any aliens at all  picard season 2 saw the borg queen  manipulating dr agnes gerardi and the  queen's motives were anything but noble  trapped in the 21st century and  imprisoned in one mind agnes and the  queen slowly merged into a single  sinister new hybrid would agnes become  the first borg queen and birth the  cyborg race in 2024 would she end up  creating the borg in the 21st century as  seven of nine feared not quite at the  urging of doradi the borg queen slowly  comes around and the two create a merged  personality with a new goal to save  wayward dying souls and resurrect them  as a new kind of borg collective with  our minds joined as one  we could be more  the newborg would be built on  cooperation and salvation not  assimilation in 2024 the gerardi queen  takes la sirena and leaves for parts  unknown the next time we see her in the  25th century she has a new massive  starship and is asking admiral picard  about joining the united federation of  planets that's all great but the  question remains what was the jaradi  queen doing for the past 400 years are  all of the borg terrors of the past  retconned into a separate timeline now  was she hiding in a distant part of the  galaxy to avoid disrupting the timeline  did she build a collective elsewhere did  she take part in galactic affairs we've  never seen there's now a 400 year gap  that needs a little explaining perhaps  the biggest unanswered question of the  bunch closes out the finale after the  combined efforts of the new borg and the  federation fleet prevent a disaster a  unique anomaly is created in the form of  a trans warp conduit seven of nine  recognizes it right away and notes that  it's unlike any she has seen before and  that's notable given her lengthy  experience with borg transwarp conduits  picard wonders who created the conduit  implying that this was not a natural  phenomenon its creation confounds even  the new borg queen but she knows that  it's a threat it's an ominous closing  message but if there's one question  likely to be resolved in season 3 it's  this one and it looks like picard will  need the help of his former enterprise  crew if he's going to discover the  answer the entire cast of the next  generation is joining the final season  of picard  [Music]

